## Bench.cpp/Rows
a handle numbered, then a row -> the next handle is #1 (was #1)
a row holding a newline, a return and a mark -> kept ["a\\nb\\r\\x1ec"]
drop, reverse, repeat 3, a row -> count 1, kept [], reverse true, repeat 3
keep, two rows and a skip -> count 2, kept ["one", "two"]

## Bench.cpp/Rows::skip
a row after a skip
a row after quiet, which made 1

## Bench.cpp/thrown
an int -> throws something not a std::exception
bad_alloc -> throws bad_alloc
bad_array_new_length -> throws bad_alloc
bad_function_call -> throws exception
bad_optional_access -> throws bad_optional_access
bad_variant_access -> throws bad_variant_access
domain_error -> throws domain_error: "a"
exception -> throws exception
filesystem_error -> throws filesystem_error
format_error -> throws runtime_error: "a"
invalid_argument -> throws invalid_argument: "a"
ios_base::failure -> throws system_error
length_error -> throws length_error: "a"
logic_error -> throws logic_error: "a"
nothing -> threw nothing
out_of_range -> throws out_of_range: "a"
overflow_error -> throws overflow_error: "a"
range_error -> throws range_error: "a"
runtime_error -> throws runtime_error: "a"
system_error -> throws system_error
underflow_error -> throws underflow_error: "a"

